// Run.ZC - launch entry point.
//
// Two stages. RunLib.ZC builds the library; this file builds the app shell and
// starts it. They are deliberately not one compile: a single 40+ file unit
// faults at run time (general protection in library code that is itself
// correct). Each ExeFile is a separate compile that completes and releases
// before the next starts, and the symbols it defines stay live in this task.
//
// RunLib.ZC documents the include order, which is load-bearing: ZealC is a
// single-pass compiler, so a file can reference symbols only from an earlier one.

Cd(__DIR__);;

"UT99 build:\n";

ExeFile("RunLib");
ExeFile("RunLib2");

"  .. UT99\n";
#include "UT99"

UT99;

"\nType $$LTBLUE$$UTTest;$$FG$$ to run the data-layer self-check.\n";
